      "channelId": "UCfetJpmQH2XpFj8uFgWsezw",
      "title": "Rendering large lists with react-virtualized or react-window",
      "description": "If you use React and need to display large lists of data efficiently, you may be familiar with react-virtualized. It's a windowing library by Brian Vaughn that renders only the items currently visible in a list (within a scrolling \"viewport\"). This means you don't need to pay the cost of thousands of rows of data being rendered at once. react-window is a recent rewrite with a focus on being smaller, faster and more easily tree-shakeable.\n\nhttps://bvaughn.github.io/react-virtualized/\nhttps://react-window.now.sh/",
